# SYNTHETIC fixture. Not a captured sweep.
# Hand-built to render literals that carry HTML markup, which no captured
# sweep does and no endpoint in this project's registry has ever returned.
#
# Why the literals and not the IRIs. An IRI cannot contain '<', '>' or '"'
# at all, and pyoxigraph rejects one that tries, so a class IRI or an
# endpoint IRI is a value that CANNOT carry markup onto the page. The values
# that can are the literals, and three of them reach the page verbatim:
# dqv:value (shown as recorded whenever the verdict is not one of the six,
# and written into data-verdict), sw:notMeasuredReason (written into
# data-declined and into the state text beside the chip) and
# prov:generatedAtTime. They arrive from whatever N-Quads web/load_run.py was
# handed, which is not something this tier controls.
#
# The two values below are the ordinary attribute-breakout and
# tag-injection shapes: each opens with a double quote to close whatever
# attribute it lands in, then opens an element. Jinja's autoescaping is what
# stops them, and web/tests/test_page.py asserts the escaped result rather
# than the fixture, so switching autoescaping off for either channel fails.
#
# dqv:value is also NOT one of the six verdicts, so the page draws it in the
# unrecognised state and shows it as recorded. That is deliberate: relabelling
# a value this build does not know would hide what the store holds.
#
# 15 quads, one run graph (urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-23T00:00:00Z), one
# endpoint, one dqv:QualityMeasurement whose value carries markup, one
# sw:NotMeasured whose reason carries markup, and no sw:ContentSample.
